# SRM v1 Protocol Draft

## English Version

### Purpose

SRM (Simple Routing Module) v1 is a lightweight binary protocol designed for communication between a master node (typically Raspberry Pi) and one or more slave nodes (typically STM32 boards).

The protocol is designed to be:

* Simple to implement
* Easy to debug
* Expandable for future peripherals and nodes
* Independent from the physical transport layer
* Compatible with RS485, UART, USB serial, TCP tunnels, and future transports

---

## Design Goals

* Support one master and multiple slave nodes
* Support node addressing
* Support request/response model
* Support ACK/NACK and retries
* Support future expansion
* Keep parser logic simple on STM32
* Allow easy debugging through ASCII tools

---

## Node Roles

* Master node: Raspberry Pi
* Slave nodes: STM32 modules

### Suggested Node IDs

| Node ID     | Meaning                      |
| ----------- | ---------------------------- |
| 0x00        | Invalid / Reserved           |
| 0x01        | Raspberry Master             |
| 0x10 - 0x7F | Slave Nodes                  |
| 0xF0 - 0xFE | Service / Bootloader / Debug |
| 0xFF        | Broadcast                    |

Example:

* Slave1 = 0x10
* Slave2 = 0x11
* LCD Module = 0x20
* Stepper Module = 0x30

---

## Frame Format

```text
SOF | VER | FLAGS | SRC | DST | CMD | SEQ | LEN | PAYLOAD | CRC16
```

### Field Description

| Field   | Size        | Description                                        |
| ------- | ----------- | -------------------------------------------------- |
| SOF     | 1 byte      | Start of Frame, fixed value 0xAA                   |
| VER     | 1 byte      | Protocol version, currently 0x01                   |
| FLAGS   | 1 byte      | Frame flags                                        |
| SRC     | 1 byte      | Source node ID                                     |
| DST     | 1 byte      | Destination node ID                                |
| CMD     | 1 byte      | Command ID                                         |
| SEQ     | 1 byte      | Sequence number                                    |
| LEN     | 1 byte      | Payload length                                     |
| PAYLOAD | 0-255 bytes | Command-specific data                              |
| CRC16   | 2 bytes     | CRC16-CCITT over the entire frame except CRC field |

Recommended maximum payload for v1:

* 64 bytes

---

## Flags

| Bit | Name         | Meaning                   |
| --- | ------------ | ------------------------- |
| 0   | ACK_REQUIRED | Receiver must acknowledge |
| 1   | IS_ACK       | This frame is an ACK      |
| 2   | IS_NACK      | This frame is a NACK      |
| 3   | IS_RESPONSE  | This frame is a response  |
| 4   | BROADCAST    | Broadcast frame           |
| 5-7 | Reserved     | Future use                |

---

## CRC

SRM v1 uses:

* CRC16-CCITT-FALSE
* Polynomial: 0x1021
* Initial value: 0xFFFF

---

## Error Codes

| Code | Meaning         |
| ---- | --------------- |
| 0x01 | CRC Error       |
| 0x02 | Unknown Command |
| 0x03 | Invalid Length  |
| 0x04 | Invalid Payload |
| 0x05 | Busy            |
| 0x06 | Not Supported   |
| 0x07 | Internal Error  |
| 0x08 | Timeout         |

---

## Suggested Command Map

| Range       | Purpose                             |
| ----------- | ----------------------------------- |
| 0x00 - 0x1F | Core Protocol                       |
| 0x20 - 0x3F | GPIO / LED / Generic Control        |
| 0x40 - 0x5F | I2C / EEPROM / LCD                  |
| 0x60 - 0x7F | Motion / Stepper / Actuator         |
| 0x80 - 0xBF | Device Specific                     |
| 0xC0 - 0xFF | Reserved / Bootloader / Diagnostics |

### Core Commands

| CMD  | Name                 |
| ---- | -------------------- |
| 0x01 | PING                 |
| 0x02 | GET_INFO             |
| 0x03 | GET_STATUS           |
| 0x04 | RESET_NODE           |
| 0x05 | SET_NODE_ID          |
| 0x06 | GET_PROTOCOL_VERSION |

---

## Example PING Request

```text
AA 01 01 01 10 01 22 00 CRC_L CRC_H
```

Meaning:

* Master 0x01 sends PING to slave 0x10
* ACK required
* Sequence number 0x22

